From Caribbean cities to Antarctica, this series follows my backpacking journey through Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Bolivia, Chile, Argentina, Uruguay, Paraguay and Brazil. This is Part I: Backpacking Colombia & Ecuador.

---

## Colombia

#### Cartagena

Cartagena is a Caribbean port city whose wealth came from shipping silver and gold from South America to Spain. Protected by huge walls and forts built against pirates, it remains one of the best preserved colonial cities in the Americas. Backpackers pass through for its history, nightlife and nearby islands.

